// REJECTS: Field 'pattern' is required
//
// A Service requires pattern, documentation and execution. The grammar's body is an
// unordered `( ... )*`, so NOTHING in the parse tree makes any of them mandatory -- the
// requirement is enforced afterwards by the walker, naming the field.
//
// This is the class of rule a generated parser misses entirely: the .g4 is satisfied, the
// tree builds, and only ServiceParseTreeWalker refuses.
###Service
Service fixture::neg::NoPattern
{
   documentation: 'no pattern';
   execution: Single
   {
      query: |fixture::neg::Person.all();
      mapping: fixture::neg::Mapping;
      runtime: fixture::neg::Runtime;
   }
}
